                                                                                
 Usage: opentide share retract [OPTIONS]                                        
                                                                                
 Unpublish a shared event, or delete it when `--delete --yes` is set.           
                                                                                
╭─ Options ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ --target         <str>  Destination block name. Repeatable.                  │
│ --uuid           <str>  Limit to these object UUIDs.                         │
│ --type           <str>  Limit to threat, objective, or rule.                 │
│ --file           <str>  Limit to these object files.                         │
│ --delete                Delete the remote event instead of unpublishing it.  │
│ --yes                   Confirm --delete.                                    │
│ --workers        <int>  Parallel object workers for one destination.         │
│                         [default: 1]                                         │
│ --help                  Show this message and exit.                          │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯

 Examples
   $ opentide share retract --uuid <uuid>
